      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1dcbd422ce1c08ad63056226e33ebe51c97daa5b11912e519ec0518d112832d0",
      "text": "Day 5 · 07:00 breakfast · 08:00 jungle walk and visit to a caboclo’s house, learning how manioc flour is prepared · 12:00 lunch · 15:00 visit to the village of Acajatuba, whose people live from manioc plantations, fishing and fruits such as tucumã, cupuaçu and açaí, as well as rubber and Brazil-nut trees, and learn how they make crafts with natural jungle seeds · 19:00 farewell dinner · 20:00 explore the riverbank by searchlight to spot caimans, and sometimes nighthawks, snakes and frogs.\n\n**Meeting of the Waters**\n\nOptional excursion. Price: $150 per person. Duration: approximately 8 hours.",
      "provenance": {
